{"name":"Windy City","hex":"#88a3c2","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Windy City","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Nickname for Chicago: a city in Illinois, United States.","Nickname for Wellington: the capital city of New Zealand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Windy_City"}],"entries":[{"title":"Windy City (nickname)","blocks":[{"text":"The city of Chicago has been known by many nicknames, but it is most widely recognized as the \"Windy City\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif/330px-En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windy_City_(nickname)"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City"},{"title":"Chicago","blocks":[{"text":"Chicago is the most populous city in the U.S. state of Illinois and in the Midwestern United States. Located on the western shore of Lake Michigan, it is the third-most populous city in the United States and the fifth-most populous city in North America, with a population of 2.74 million at the 2020 census. The Chicago metropolitan area has approximately 9.62 million residents according to the 2020 census and is the third-largest metropolitan statistical area in the country and part of the fourth-largest combined statistical area in the United States, spanning 19 counties in three states and with a population of nearly 10 million. Chicago is the county seat of Cook County, the second-most populous county in the U.S."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg/330px-Chicago_River_ferry_b.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chicago"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif/500px-En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif/500px-En-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This newspaper article was published by the Cleveland Gazette in 1885.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEn-Chicago-CiteSourceWindyCityHistory01.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum